  "static_review": {
    "blocking_findings": [],
    "resolved_findings": [
      "Full-text labels no longer claim arbitrary field searching in the Web API.",
      "Search options use one state-controlled conditional panel, preserving expansion and preferences across disconnect/reconnect.",
      "A Search options icon in the search row preserves default catalog height and paging visibility; additional height is allocated only to the expanded panel.",
      "The page summary uses Expanded with one-line ellipsis to leave navigation controls their width.",
      "Each catalog query test tap checks immediately for Flutter exceptions; accepted coverage includes 320, 360 and 420 logical-pixel widths and the existing default paging regression."
    ],
    "final_diff_assessment": "The final delta since 1180537c replaces the ExpansionTile header with a Search options icon and conditional panel, factors layout allocation into _catalogMinHeight, and strengthens widget exception assertions. Query, resolver and document mutation semantics remain unchanged. No unresolved static correctness issue was found in this scope.",
    "verified_design": [
      "Validated complete Zotero URIs establish transitive aliases; matching keys or CSL IDs alone do not merge scopes.",
      "Representative source identities are deterministic in first-declared order, preferring eligible numeric identities online; failures do not retry through aliases.",
      "Refresh and bibliography limits count resolved components; the resolver bounds unique aliases at 10,000.",
      "Alias declarations in custom or snapshot-free citations can bridge components; refresh mutation remains restricted to supported basic-author-year fields.",
      "Refresh preserves citation identities, URI arrays, locators, affixes and unknown citation metadata while staging fetched CSL updates; existing controller transaction and DOCX behavior remain in the accepted test cohort.",
      "Unsubmitted text does not affect either paging direction; option and scope changes submit the current draft from offset zero.",
      "Source/disconnect transitions retain query preferences and invalidate prior catalog generations; asynchronous mutation guards remain in place."
    ]
  },
